{"metadata":{"title":"halign","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLOtherDirectionV6halignAA18MXLLeftCenterRightOSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"halign","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The most typical case is for credits, such as:","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlotherdirection\/halign"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherDirection"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"halign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Words and music by Pat Songwriter","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Typically this type of credit is aligned to the right, so that the position information refers to the right-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"most part of the text. But in this example, the text is center-justified, not right-justified.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The halign attribute is used in these situations. If it is not present, its value is the same as for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"justify attribute. For elements where a justify attribute is not allowed, the default is implementation-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dependent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"halign"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherDirection\/halign","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherDirection":{"title":"MXLOtherDirection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlotherdirection","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOtherDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherDirection","abstract":[{"text":"The other-direction type is used to define any direction symbols not yet in the MusicXML format. The smufl","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute can be used to specify a particular direction symbol, allowing application interoperability without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requiring every SMuFL glyph to have a MusicXML element equivalent. Using the other-direction type without the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smufl attribute allows for extended representation, though without application interoperability.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOtherDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherDirection/halign":{"title":"halign","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlotherdirection\/halign","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/I